Subject: [PATCH] seam: pin IsBufferRowInViewport, and retract a wrong
 justification

Adds ControlCoreTests::TestIsBufferRowInViewport (viewport bounds at the
bottom and scrolled back) and TestIsBufferRowInViewportAltBuffer.

Writing the second test disproved the reason the first commit gave for
this method existing. That commit claimed ICoreState::ScrollOffset +
ViewHeight could not substitute, because Terminal::_VisibleStartIndex()
short-circuits to 0 in the alt buffer while GetViewport().Top() does
not. That was read out of the source and never measured. Measured, they
agree everywhere: main buffer at the bottom 21/21, main buffer scrolled
back 5/5, alt buffer 0/0. GetViewport() returns the *visible* viewport.

The implementation does not change - it calls the same GetViewport() the
escape did, so it is faithful regardless - and the real justification
stands on its own: the escape read both bounds under a single console
lock, and two property reads would take two. Only the stated reason was
wrong. Comments in ControlCore.cpp and IControlCore.idl are corrected,
and the alt-buffer test now asserts the agreement so a future divergence
fails rather than becoming folklore.

